; SKIPDISP takes one required int expression
; (GameProc/Function/FunctionIdentifier.cs:317, INT_EXPRESSION), sets the skip
; state from `value != 0` and puts that new state in RESULT
; (GameProc/Process.ScriptProc.cs:571-578).
;
; It must take that argument out of the command argument list. Reading the
; value stack directly popped the *caller's* frame and left this command's own
; argument behind, so every SKIPDISP corrupted the stack — this fixture passing
; also means the harness' end-of-run "stack is empty" check passed.
@SYSTEM_TITLE
PRINTFORML start

SKIPDISP 1
LOCAL = RESULT
; suppressed: ISSKIP is on, so no PRINT reaches the console
PRINTL invisible-1
PRINTFORML invisible-2
SKIPDISP 0
PRINTFORML on={LOCAL} off={RESULT}

; RESULT is the *state*, not the argument: any non-zero value means on.
SKIPDISP 7
LOCAL = RESULT
SKIPDISP 0
PRINTFORML seven={LOCAL}

; ISSKIP reads back the same state.
SKIPDISP 1
LOCAL = ISSKIP()
SKIPDISP 0
PRINTFORML isskip={LOCAL} now={ISSKIP()}

PRINTFORML end
